# Comprehensive Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Trustworthy Money Movement Platform — Hackathon Edition

**Document status:** Implementation-ready v1
**Target:** 2-person, 6-hour hackathon
**Deployment:** Fully local through Docker
**Primary emphasis:** Backend correctness, concurrency, resiliency, auditability and scalability design
**Frontend:** Next.js PWA + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn/ui
**Currency:** BDT only
**Money:** Simulated funds; no banks, cards or real payment rails

The product should be judged as a **small, trustworthy financial system**, not as a large feature-heavy wallet. That aligns closely with the original challenge, which asks the team to think beyond CRUD, consider simultaneous activity and future growth, and build a small but thoughtful closed ecosystem rather than a complete banking platform. 

---

# 1. Product vision

> **Build the smallest money-movement platform in which users can trust that every taka moves correctly, exactly once, to the intended person—even when requests are duplicated, multiple transfers happen simultaneously, an application server dies, or parts of the system become unavailable.**

The visible application should be deliberately simple.

