# 14. Idempotency design

This is P0.

Frontend generates:

```text
UUIDv4
```

before sending.

Example:

```http
POST /api/v1/transfers

Idempotency-Key:
02b385e2-...
```

Store:

```text
idempotency_records

id
user_id
idempotency_key
request_hash
resource_type
resource_id
status_code
response_body
created_at
expires_at
```

Unique constraint:

```text
UNIQUE(user_id, idempotency_key)
```

### Same key + same request

Return original result.

```text
50 calls
same key
same request

→ one transfer
→ 49 safe replays
```

### Same key + different payload

Return:

```text
409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
```

Stripe also compares incoming request parameters against the original parameters when an idempotency key is reused. ([Stripe Docs][6])

