# 32. Why three backend replicas?

Not to claim:

> “We support 10 million users.”

Instead prove:

> “Application instances are stateless. Financial correctness does not depend on which application process receives the request.”

Request 1 can hit:

```text
API-1
```

while request 2 hits:

```text
API-3
```

and PostgreSQL still controls the account locks.

This is the scalable architectural property you actually need to demonstrate.

