# 35. PWA offline policy

BalanceLoop's offline-first design shows the value of keeping history and actions resilient under connectivity problems, but because our application actually moves money, offline semantics must be stricter. BalanceLoop can queue settlements and synchronize later without double-counting; our application should never claim a financial transfer completed without server authority. 

## Recommended hackathon policy

When online:

```text
Full application
```

When offline:

```text
App shell                     ✓

previous history              ✓

last known balance            ✓
"Last updated 10:42"

Send money                    ✗

Pay request                   ✗
```

Display:

> You're offline. Reconnect before sending money securely.

M-PESA has publicly explored offline-oriented app functionality, showing that poor connectivity is a legitimate mobile-money UX concern, but our prototype should use a safer read-only offline model rather than attempt deferred money execution. ([Safaricom][9])

