## Final pitch

> **We built a trustworthy money-movement system inspired by the reliability requirements of large mobile financial services. The application itself is intentionally simple, but every transfer is atomic, concurrency-safe, idempotent and auditable. We then run multiple stateless backend replicas locally with Docker and deliberately subject the platform to duplicate requests, simultaneous spending, server failure and network faults. After every scenario, an independent reconciliation engine proves that no account went negative, no transfer was duplicated and no money was created or lost.**

